.TH MAKEWHATIS 8 "September 16, 2026"
.UC 2
.SH NAME
makewhatis \- remake the database for the whatis and apropos commands
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B makewhatis
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B makewhatis
is a shell script that uses the \fBsed\fP(1) program 
\fI/usr/man/makewhatis.sed\fP to create the whatis database in /usr/man
from the manual sections in /usr/man/cat*.
The relevant text is extracted extracted from each manpage and sorted
.sp
The database is used by whatis(8) and apropos(8).
.SH FILES
.DT
/usr/man/whatis		constructed data base
.SH SEE ALSO
sed(1), whatis(1), apropos(1)
